Node drain stuck indefinitely due to unresponsive terminating pod

Step-by-Step Fix:
Identify the Stuck Pod
kubectl get pods -A --field-selector spec.nodeName=<NODE_NAME>
Check pod status:
kubectl describe pod <pod-name> -n <namespace>
Check PodDisruptionBudget (Very Common)
kubectl get pdb -A
kubectl describe pdb <pdb-name> -n <namespace>
Force Delete the Pod (Most Effective)
kubectl delete pod <pod-name> -n <namespace> \
  --grace-period=0 --force
Remove Blocking Finalizers:
kubectl get pod <pod-name> -n <namespace> -o yaml
kubectl patch pod <pod-name> -n <namespace> \
  -p '{"metadata":{"finalizers":[]}}' --type=merge
